## Why This Is Asked
This checks understanding of streaming data structures and complexity trade-offs for maintaining order statistics under batch updates.

## Key Concepts
- Running median via two heaps
- Per-element insert cost and batch amortization
- Memory growth with total elements

## Code Example
```javascript
class MedianMaintainer {
  constructor() {
    this.low = new MaxHeap();
    this.high = new MinHeap();
  }
  add(x) {
    if (this.low.isEmpty() || x <= this.low.peek()) this.low.push(x);
    else this.high.push(x);
    // rebalance
    if (this.low.size() > this.high.size() + 1) this.high.push(this.low.pop());
    else if (this.high.size() > this.low.size()) this.low.push(this.high.pop());
  }
  median() {
    if (this.low.size() === this.high.size()) return (this.low.peek() + this.high.peek()) / 2;
    return this.low.peek();
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How does varying batch size B affect latency and memory?
- How would you extend to handle sliding windows or duplicates efficiently?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests real-world streaming analytics: maintaining a dynamic feature (distinct count) under batched updates with tight per-batch guarantees. It probes data structures (circular buffers, counters), amortized reasoning, and practical optimizations under constrained space. 

## Key Concepts
- Sliding window maintenance
- Distinct counting with frequency map
- Amortized analysis under batched updates
- Space-conscious data structures and optimizations

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation skeleton demonstrating the core idea
class WindowDistinct {
  constructor(W) {
    this.W = W;
    this.buf = new Array(W);
    this.freq = new Map();
    this.head = 0; // points to oldest element
    this.size = 0;
    this.distinct = 0;
  }
  init(arr) {
    for (let i = 0; i < this.W; i++) this.push(arr[i]);
  }
  push(x) {
    if (this.size < this.W) this.size++;
    else {
      this.pop();
    }
    this.buf[this.head] = x;
    this.head = (this.head + 1) % this.W;
    const c = (this.freq.get(x) || 0) + 1;
    this.freq.set(x, c);
    if (c === 1) this.distinct++;
  }
  pop() {
    const idx = (this.head) % this.W;
    const y = this.buf[idx];
    const c = this.freq.get(y) - 1;
    if (c === 0) this.freq.delete(y);
    else this.freq.set(y, c);
    if (c === 0) this.distinct--;
  }
  batchUpdate(batch) {
    for (const x of batch) this.push(x);
  }
  query() {
    return this.distinct;
  }
}
```
